.TH EVNIA\-PRECISION\-CENTER 1 2026-09-27 "1.13.0-linux.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
evnia\-precision\-center \- control centre for Philips Evnia monitors (unofficial offline port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B evnia\-precision\-center
.RB [ \-\-openAsHidden ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B evnia\-precision\-center
is an unofficial, offline Linux port of Evnia Precision Center 1.13.0.
It adjusts a Philips Evnia monitor: picture modes (SmartImage), game
settings, input, audio, system settings, profiles, the dashboard overlay
and Ambiglow lighting.
It reaches the monitor over its USB upstream cable (USB\-DDC bridge and
Ambiglow controller) or, without that cable, over DDC/CI on the graphics
card's i2c buses.
The program makes no network connection.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user; starting it again shows the running
window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-openAsHidden
Start without showing the window, reachable from the tray icon.
The login autostart entry uses it.
Without a tray host (for example GNOME without the AppIndicator
extension) the window is shown anyway.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EVNIA_ENE_FRAME_BURST
Experimental: when set to
.BR 1 ,
Ambiglow "Follow video" sends each LED update to the Ambiglow controller
as one USB transfer instead of six, whatever the "Fast LED upload
(experimental)" checkbox of the Ambiglow page says (it is then shown
ticked and greyed out). The checkbox is the usual way to switch it; its
setting is kept in
.IR ~/.config/evnia/config.json .
Untested on real monitors; untick the checkbox, or unset the variable,
if the LEDs misbehave. A controller that refuses the single transfer is
logged, and after three failures in a row the six transfers are used
again.
.TP
.B EVNIA_MOCK_MONITOR
For testing: when set to a model name such as
.BR 34M2C8600 ,
the program runs against a simulated monitor of that model and opens no
real hardware.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the files below (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/evnia/
Program settings
.RI ( config.json )
and logs
.RI ( logs/ ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/EvniaServe/
Themes, profiles, macros and the backend logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/evnia\-precision\-center.desktop
Login autostart entry, written when "Start with the system" is enabled.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/evnia\-debug\-open.tmp
When this file exists at start, the log level is debug and Alt+Shift+M
opens the developer tools.
The file is removed when the program exits.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70\-evnia\-precision\-center.rules
Grants the user at the local seat access to the monitor's USB\-DDC bridge
(2109:8884), its Ambiglow controller (0cf2:a201) and the i2c buses of
display adapters, except their SMBus and AMDGPU SMU buses.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/modules\-load.d/evnia\-precision\-center\-i2c.conf
Loads the i2c\-dev module at boot.
.SH NOTES
.B Profile \(-> Reset
and
.B Settings \(-> Factory reset
also restore the monitor's own factory settings: like the Windows
application they send the DDC/CI command "Restore factory defaults"
(VCP 0x04 = 1), so every OSD picture setting of the monitor returns to its
factory value.
Factory reset also deletes the program's themes, profiles, macros and
settings in
.I ~/.config/EvniaServe
(the logs are kept).
.PP
Removing the package leaves the files in the users' home directories in
place.
.PP
More information, including desktop\-specific notes, is in
.IR /usr/share/doc/evnia\-precision\-center/README.Debian.gz .
